<!--
  TEMPLATE. Copy this file to `Directory.Build.props` (same folder) and edit the two paths.
  That copy is gitignored; this one is tracked so the setup is discoverable.

  WHY THIS EXISTS
  The project resolves roughly 290 assembly references out of a Schedule I install through
  $(S1Dir), and that path is different on every machine. Hardcoding it in the csproj means the
  build only ever works for one person - which is exactly the state this file replaced.

  WHAT TO POINT IT AT
  Schedule I ships in two flavours and each configuration needs its own copy of the game:

    MONO    -> an install with `Schedule I_Data\Managed\Assembly-CSharp.dll` and no GameAssembly.dll
    IL2CPP  -> an install with `GameAssembly.dll` next to `Schedule I.exe`

  MELONLOADER HAS TO BE INSTALLED INTO EACH OF THEM, and it is not optional:

    MONO    needs $(S1Dir)\MelonLoader\net35\0Harmony.dll
    IL2CPP  needs $(S1Dir)\MelonLoader\Il2CppAssemblies\*  - these are GENERATED, so the game
            has to be launched once with MelonLoader installed before the folder exists.

  A build with a wrong or unprepared path fails on the reference resolution, and the csproj
  raises a readable error naming the missing folder rather than several hundred CS0246s.

  USE A COPY YOU DO NOT PLAY ON. The IL2CPP configuration copies its output DLL into
  $(S1Dir)\Mods\ after every build, so pointing this at your everyday, mod-managed install
  means your builds land in it.
-->
<Project>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)' == 'MONO' And '$(S1Dir)' == ''">
    <S1Dir>C:\Path\To\Your\Schedule I Mono</S1Dir>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)' == 'IL2CPP' And '$(S1Dir)' == ''">
    <S1Dir>C:\Path\To\Your\Schedule I IL2CPP</S1Dir>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
